    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside profile of **Junior Caminero**, who earns our top efficiency score of 75.43. Despite a slightly unfavorable park, **Junior Caminero** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Bassitt, combined with the favorable lineup protection of hitting in the cleanup spot. **Yordan Alvarez** follows closely with a 71.66 score; his elite 0.464 xwOBA makes him a mandatory start regardless of the matchup against George Kirby, though his platoon edge today provides an extra cushion. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** remains a crucial engine for our stolen base objectives. His 64.19 score is buoyed by his ability to exploit the pitcher's slow delivery, keeping him firmly in the lineup as our primary speed catalyst.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles, most notably with **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, whose 62.44 score is tempered by a significant 15% penalty due to his platoon disadvantage against Liberatore. However, his leadoff spot remains too valuable to ignore. We nearly slotted **Chase Meidroth** into the utility role, but his 39.26 score narrowly missed our 40.0 floor, leaving him on the bench as the most difficult omission of the day. The primary risk remains the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich**. While both project for solid contributions, we are banking on favorable weather and confirmed order placements to ensure their projected production against Yamamoto holds. With **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Lars Nootbaar** unavailable, we are leaning heavily on **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** to provide middle-order power against Matz to keep our HR and RBI pace competitive.",
